id: pm-rl-lintruntime
title: Keep retained runtime artifacts outside authored-source lint
description: "Local npm run lint traverses ignored .agents/pm/runtime execution snapshots and rejects generated packaged declarations there for inline type imports. scripts/eslint.config.ts ignores only root dist, coverage and node_modules. Identical authored sources pass lint in a clean worktree. Preserve retained raw-run evidence and keep the authored source scope and all release thresholds unchanged; define a precise runtime-artifact ignore boundary with regression coverage."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 3
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T17:42:54.342Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T19:39:06.788Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: A retained packaged declaration under ignored .agents/pm/runtime does not alter authored-source lint results; authored sources and tests remain linted at unchanged strictness; raw execution evidence is preserved.
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T18:03:11.793Z",codex-agent,"Discovered while validating PR #94: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/94 . Retained ignored execution snapshots trigger the strict inline-import rule in generated packaged declarations, while byte-identical authored sources pass lint and all three complete release variants in clean CI. This follow-up remains separate from corpus output safety. Preserve retained evidence and every authored-source rule/coverage threshold."
  "2026-10-22T19:39:06.787Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced during PR #97 sealed-evidence review: unmodified npm run check linted generated index.d.ts beneath a retained ignored .agents/pm/runtime/live-meta acceptance output and reported two compiler-generated inline type imports. This is the existing runtime-artifact lint-scope issue, not authored source. Preserved the task-owned synthetic acceptance output outside the package worktree and reran unchanged checks. No lint policy, threshold, fixture data or source was deleted or excluded in the review fix; this follow-up remains open."
